                            CONTRIBUTING
Changes require an RFC (request for comments) before a PR. Post your proposal to
the engineering team at contact@podomy.com.

This includes new subsystems, protocol changes, and architectural
decisions. PRs opened without a prior group discussion will be redirected there
before code review.

Use GitHub Issues for bugs and actionable tasks. Tag issues with
good-first-issue if they are suitable for newcomers.

                         Review Expectations

Small PR (bugfix)       3 business days
Normal PR               7 days
RFC                     7 days

If maintainers cannot meet the window, they will say so. Silence is
not a no.

                          Getting Started
Prerequisites  Go >=1.26.3 (go.work:1) and golangci-lint v2.14.0
+               Install: https://golangci-lint.run/welcome/install/

1. Build        go build ./...
2. Verify       go run ./check/   # go mod tidy (root, sdk, cmd/weld with GOWORK=off) + git diff --exit-code + golangci-lint fmt --diff (gofumpt/goimports @.golangci.yml:7) + goheader check + golangci-lint run + go vet + go test, per module
3. Test         go test ./...   # already in verify
4. Pick an issue or go over the code

0. Setup        make setup sets git config core.hooksPath .githooks so the
verify script runs on every commit via .githooks/pre-commit. It never
leaves the machine; a commit is done when the hook passes. Run once
per fresh clone.

5. Send an RFC to contact@podomy.com if the change is not small
6. Submit a PR
